          %p
          %h2#section_Introduction Introduction
          %p
            A
            %em finite set
            is, roughly speaking, a
            = succeed "\u00A0with" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/element"} elements
          %p
            Classically, the finite sets are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+presentable+object"} finitely presentable objects
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            %em finitely presented
            is properly interpreted, see there for details.
          %p
            The category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FinSet"} FinSet
            of finite sets and functions between them is a prime example of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elementary+topos"} elementary topos
            which is not a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorics"} combinatorics
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+types"} structure types
          %p
          %h2#section_Definitions Definitions
          %p
          %h3#section_Standard_definition Standard definition
          %p We can for example make the following definition.
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong finite set
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              for which there exists a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
              between
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              and the set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi k
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi k
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [n] \coloneqq \{k\in \mathbb{N} | k\lt n\}
              for some
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n\in \mathbb{N}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
              is the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+number"} natural numbers
          %p#Constructivist
          %h3#section_Finiteness_constructively_and_internally Finiteness constructively and internally
          %p
          %h4#section_Variations Variations
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                A set is
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite"} finite
                (for emphasis
                %strong Bishop-finite
                or
                = succeed ")" do
                  %strong
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi B
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                    \-finite
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
                with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [n]
                for some
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+number"} natural number
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %li
              %p
                A set is
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subfinite"} subfinite
                (or
                = succeed ")" do
                  %strong
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mover
                            %mi B
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde{B}
                    \-finite
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injection"} injection
                into some finite set
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [n]
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
                of a finite set.
            %li
              %p
                A set is
                %strong finitely indexed
                (or
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kuratowski-finite"} Kuratowski-finite
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi K
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
                    \-finite
                = succeed ")" do
                  %em subfinite
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjection"} surjection
                from some finite set
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [n]
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+set"} quotient set
                of a finite set.
            %li
              %p
                A set is
                %strong subfinitely indexed
                (or
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kuratowski-subfinite"} Kuratowski-subfinite
                or
                = succeed ")" do
                  %strong
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mover
                            %mi K
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde{K}
                    \-finite
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subquotient+set"} subquotient set
                of a finite set.
            %li
              %p
                A set
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dedekind-finite"} Dedekind-finite
                if it satisfies one of the following:
              %ul
                %li
                  any
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injection"} injection
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\hookrightarrow X
                  must be a
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
                %li
                  for any function
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi ℕ
                        %mo →
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon \mathbb{N} \to X
                  from the
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ,
                        %mi m
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n,m
                  with
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ≠
                        %mi m
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \ne m
                  such that
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi m
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(n) = f(m)
              %p
                In contrast to the previous three notions, Dedekind-finite
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinite+sets"} infinite sets
                can coexist with
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excluded+middle"} excluded middle
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countable+choice"} countable choice
                suffices to banish them. The above two versions of Dedekind-finiteness are equivalent with excluded middle, but constructively they may differ. In addition, there are other forms of Dedekind-finiteness that are strictly stronger even with excluded middle; see
                %a{:href => "https://mathoverflow.net/q/410013/"} this MO question
                for instance.
          %p In constructive mathematics, one is usually interested in the finite sets, although the finitely indexed sets are also sometimes useful, as are the Dedekind-finite sets in the second sense.
          %p
          %h4#section_Properties_and_relationships Properties and relationships
          %p Of course, we have
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi finitely
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi indexed
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⇗
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⇘
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi finite
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi subfinitely
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi indexed
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⇘
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⇗
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi subfinite
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{ &amp; &amp; finitely\;indexed\\
                  \&amp; \neArrow &amp; &amp; \seArrow\\
                  finite &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; subfinitely\;indexed\\
                  \&amp; \seArrow &amp; &amp; \neArrow\\
                  \&amp; &amp; subfinite }
          %p Moreover:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Finite and subfinite sets have
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decidable+equality"} decidable equality
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complement"} complemented
                subset of a finite set is finite.
            %li
              %p Finite sets are closed under finite limits and colimits.
            %li
              %p A finitely indexed set with decidable equality must actually be finite. For it is then the quotient of a decidable equivalence relation, hence a coequalizer of finite sets. In particular, a set which is both finitely indexed and subfinite must be finite, i.e. the above “commutative square” of implications is also a “pullback”.
            %li
              %p
                In particular, a set with a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+surjection"} split surjection
                from
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [n]
                is finite, since it has both a surjection from and an injection into
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [n]
            %li
              %p
                Finite sets are always
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+object"} projective
                = succeed "\u201D" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
            %li
              %p
                However, if a finite set with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
                elements (or any set, finite or not, with at least
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
                distinct elements) is
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/choice+object"} choice
                = succeed "-indexed" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excluded+middle"} excluded middle
                for a proof).
            %li
              %p Finite sets are also Dedekind-finite (in either sense).
            %li
              %p
                If
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+category"} filtered category
                means
                = succeed "," do
                  %em admitting cocones of every Bishop-finite diagram
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+object"} finitely presented object
                in Set and it is Kuratowski-finite iff it is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+generated+object"} finitely generated object
                in Set.
          %p#Finitist
          %h4#section_Finiteness_without_infinity Finiteness without infinity
          %p
            All of the above definitions except for Dedekind-finiteness only make sense given the set of natural numbers. However, they can all be rephrased to make sense even without the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+infinity"} axiom of infinity
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+theory"} set theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers+object"} natural numbers object
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            that includes all of the finite subsets’ by requiring it to be closed under inductive operations appropriate for the sense of ‘finite’ that you want; then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is finite if and only if it is an element of all such collections. Namely, for any set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            we define the following subsets of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+set"} power set
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(S)
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(S)
              is the smallest subset of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(S)
              containing the empty set and closed under the operation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∪
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \mapsto A \cup B
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              a subset of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singleton"} singleton
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is finitely-indexed iff
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \in K(S)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(S)
              is also the free
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semilattice"} semilattice
              generated by
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde{K}(S)
              is the smallest subset of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(S)
              containing the empty set and closed under the operation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∪
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \mapsto A \cup B
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              a subset of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsingleton"} subsingleton
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is subfinitely-indexed iff
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo ∈
                      %mover
                        %mi K
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \in \tilde{K}(S)
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B(S)
              is the smallest subset of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(S)
              containing the empty set and closed under the operation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∪
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \mapsto A \cup B
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              a subset of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              a singleton in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+sets"} disjoint
              from
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is finite iff
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \in B(S)
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde{B}(S)
              is the smallest subset of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(S)
              containing the empty set and closed under the operation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∪
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \mapsto A \cup B
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              a subset of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              a subsingleton in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              disjoint from
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is subfinite iff
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo ∈
                      %mover
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \in \tilde{B}(S)
          %p
            In addition, finite sets are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decidable+subsets"} decidable subsets
            of themselves, so one could use the set of decidable subsets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mn 2
                    %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2^S
            in the definition of finite set instead of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+sets"} power sets
          %ul
            %li
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B(S)
              denote the smallest subset of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mn 2
                      %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2^S
              containing the empty set and closed under the operation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∪
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \mapsto A \cup B
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              a decidable subset of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              a singleton in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+sets"} disjoint
              from
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is finite iff
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \in B(S)
          %p The definitions of subfinite, finitely indexed, and subfinitely indexed follow from above:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                A set is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subfinite"} subfinite
                if it admits an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injection"} injection
                into some finite set.
            %li
              %p
                A set is finitely indexed if it admits a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjection"} surjection
                from some finite set.
            %li
              %p A set is subfinitely indexed if it admits a surjection from a subfinite set, or equivalently admits an injection to a finitely indexed set.
          %p#External
          %h3#section_In_a_topos In a topos
          %p
            In a topos, there are both “external” and “internal” versions of all the above notions of finiteness, depending on whether we interpret their meaning “globally” or in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} internal logic
            of the topos. See
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+object"} finite object
          %p
          %h2#section_Properties_of_the_category_of_finite_sets Properties of the category of finite sets
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FinSet"} FinSet
            of finite sets is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalent
            to that of finite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boolean+algebras"} Boolean algebras
            by the
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+set"} power set
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            %em
              %a{:href => "FinSet#OppositeCategory"} FinSet – Opposite category
            for details and see at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stone+duality"} Stone duality
            for more.
          %p
          %h2#section_Viewing_as_schemes Viewing as schemes
          %p
            Every finite set can be viewed as an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+scheme"} affine scheme
            %em finite
            coproduct of affine schemes
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %msub
                      %mi R
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec R_i
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i=1,\ldots,n
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi R
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ×
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi R
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec (R_1 \times \cdots \times R_n)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            many copies of the terminal scheme,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec \mathbb{Z}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec (\mathbb{Z}^X)
          %p
            Equipping
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            with a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+order"} total order
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integer"} integers
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mi n
                      %mo }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left\{ x_1, \ldots, x_n \right\}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            as the set of zeroes of the set of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial"} polynomials
            in one variable
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
            given by
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mi y
                      %mo −
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo −
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mi n
                      %mo }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left\{ y - x_1, \ldots, y - x_n \right\}
          %p
            Thus, one can view
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            as the affine scheme (over
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec(\mathbb{Z})
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum+of+a+commutative+ring"} commutative ring spectrum
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi I
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec\left( \mathbb{Z}[y] / I \right)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            is the ideal generated by the afore-mentioned polynomial(s). Since
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi I
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}[y] / I \simeq \mathbb{Z}^n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subscheme"} closed subscheme
            of the affine line
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec(\mathbb{Z}[y])
          %p
            One can view
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            as a ‘constant scheme’ over any other base scheme
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            by
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projection"} projection
            morphism
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \times X \to Y
          %p
          %h2#section_Related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinite+set"} infinite set
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hereditarily+finite+set"} hereditarily finite set
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FinSet"} FinSet
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+finite+subsets"} space of finite subsets
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+object"}> finite object
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+type"} finite type
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cardinality"} cardinality
                of a finite set is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+number"} finite number
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofinite+subset"} cofinite subset
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countable+ordinal"} countable ordinal
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite-dimensional+vector+space"} finite-dimensional vector space
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+homotopy+type"}> finite homotopy type
                ,
              %ul
                %li
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+CW-complex"}> finite CW-complex
                  ,
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+spectrum"} finite spectrum
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profinite+set"} profinite set
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+cover"} finite cover
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+graph"} finite graph
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+category"} finite category
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limit"}> finite limit
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-finite+limit"} L-finite limit
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+homotopy+type"}> finite homotopy type
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%CF%80-finite+homotopy+type"} π-finite homotopy type
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+finite+type"} locally finite type
          %p
          %h2#section_References References
          %p Original articles:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kazimierz+Kuratowski"}> C. Kuratowski
              ,
              %em Sur la notion d’ensemble fini
              , Fund. Math.
              %strong I
              (1920) pp.130-131. (
              %a{:href => "http://matwbn.icm.edu.pl/ksiazki/fm/fm1/fm1117.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              Wikipedia,
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Finite_set"} Finite set
          %p
            Discussion of notions of finite sets in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
          %ul
            %li#SpiwackCoquand10
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Arnaud+Spiwack"}> Arnaud Spiwack
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thierry+Coquand"} Thierry Coquand
              = succeed "," do
                %em Constructively Finite?
              = succeed "," do
                %em Contribuciones cientifícas en honor de Mirian Andrés Gómez
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://inria.hal.science/inria-00503917"} inria-00503917
          %p
            Formalization in
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalent+foundations+of+mathematics"} univalent foundations of mathematics
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dan+Frumin"}> Dan Frumin
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Herman+Geuvers"} Herman Geuvers
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L%C3%A9on+Gondelman"} Léon Gondelman
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Niels+van+der+Weide"} Niels van der Weide
              = succeed "," do
                %em Finite Sets in Homotopy Type Theory
              %em CPP 2018: Proceedings of the 7th ACM SIGPLAN International Conference on Certified Programs and Proofs
              (2018) 201–214 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1145/3167085"}> doi:10.1145/3167085
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://cs.ru.nl/~nweide/FiniteSetsInHoTT.pdf"} pdf
